Algorithem to find the roots of quadratic equation. 

Step1: Start. 
Step2:Input Coefficient a,b, and c. 
Step3:      D= b×b-(4×a×c)         
Case1: If(D>0) roots real and distinct. 
Root1: (-b+sqrt(D)) ÷ (2×a) 
Root2:(-b-sqrt(D) ÷(2×a) 
print Root1 and Root2

Case2: If(D=0), roots real and equal
Root1=Root2=-b÷(2×a) 
print Root1 and Root2
Case3:If(D<0) roots are imaginary
print"Roots are imaginary "
Step4:Stop   